{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeSK4HjFV38R58v89NqAG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MGZRwCujuTQVeJi3SJtFTw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/davidlayson/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-fta-2026-08-26-without-lessons-ledger--ll1-r2/memory/staging-debug-flag-swallows-errors.md","content":"---\nname: staging-debug-flag-swallows-errors\ndescription: Staging config with DEBUG=true silently swallowed all errors; cost ~2h of debugging on 2026-08-26\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nOn 2026-08-26 the team lost ~2 hours chasing a bug that was actually `DEBUG=true` in the staging config — with it set, errors were silently swallowed instead of surfacing. It was fixed the same day.\n\n**Why:** A config flag that hides errors looks exactly like \"the code is fine but behaving wrong,\" so it sends debugging in the wrong direction for a long time.\n\n**How to apply:** When a bug on staging presents as missing/absent errors or unexplained silent failures, check the environment config (DEBUG and similar flags) *before* digging into code paths. Consider suggesting a startup guard or CI check that fails if `DEBUG=true` in non-local environments.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2910,"cache_creation_input_tokens":485,"cache_read_input_tokens":18738,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":485},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6f9e68a-f856-4945-823f-28c61a0ff067","uuid":"898612b8-249e-4b70-b75a-628385c4425e","timestamp":"2026-08-27T00:32:43.015Z","request_id":"req_011CeSK4FbmEi2bBPy4CxtzV"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MGZRwCujuTQVeJi3SJtFTw","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/davidlayson/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-fta-2026-08-26-without-lessons-ledger--ll1-r2/memory/staging-debug-flag-swallows-errors.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6f9e68a-f856-4945-823f-28c61a0ff067","uuid":"dd3af87d-79ed-414e-840f-f5137f587733","timestamp":"2026-08-27T00:32:43.066Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/davidlayson/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-fta-2026-08-26-without-lessons-ledger--ll1-r2/memory/staging-debug-flag-swallows-errors.md","content":"---\nname: staging-debug-flag-swallows-errors\ndescription: Staging config with DEBUG=true silently swallowed all errors; cost ~2h of debugging on 2026-08-26\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: e6f9e68a-f856-4945-823f-28c61a0ff067\n  modified: 2026-08-27T00:32:43.062Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-08-26 the team lost ~2 hours chasing a bug that was actually `DEBUG=true` in the staging config — with it set, errors were silently swallowed instead of surfacing. It was fixed the same day.\n\n**Why:** A config flag that hides errors looks exactly like \"the code is fine but behaving wrong,\" so it sends debugging in the wrong direction for a long time.\n\n**How to apply:** When a bug on staging presents as missing/absent errors or unexplained silent failures, check the environment config (DEBUG and similar flags) *before* digging into code paths. Consider suggesting a startup guard or CI check that fails if `DEBUG=true` in non-local environments.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true}}
